; --historical (-H) gives each amount the value its commodity had when
; the amount was acquired, through nail_down(), which looked up the
; commodity by the symbol it prints.  For a commodity printed in quotes
; that found nothing, so nail_down() created another commodity whose
; name held the quotes, and the amount was printed as ""EXV6_DE""10
; (#3321).

P 2025/04/29 EXV6_DE $50.00

2025/04/30 Buy
    Assets:Broker                   10 "EXV6_DE" @ $48.50
    Assets:Cash

test reg -H --format '%(amount_expr)\n' Broker
10 "EXV6_DE"
end test
